title: 'rpc: cache runtime version by code hash in `CodeProvider`'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: "## Description\nOn Polkadot Asset Hub, state_call RPCs to historical\
    \ blocks can take >1s. Each call goes through CodeProvider::on_chain_runtime_version()\
    \ which accesses the executor's `RuntimeCache` \u2014 acquiring its global mutex,\
    \ performing an LRU lookup, and on a miss: reading the :code blob (~10 MB) and\
    \ recompiling WASM (1-3s, mutex held).\n\nThis PR adds a `code_hash` \u2192 `RuntimeVersion`\
    \ HashMap cache to `CodeProvider` so that `on_chain_runtime_version()` short-circuits\
    \ with a single `RwLock<HashMap>` lookup (concurrent reads on the hot path), avoiding\
    \ the `RuntimeCache` mutex entirely.\n\nThe cache is unbounded but safe \u2014\
    \ it grows by one entry per runtime upgrade.\n\nBenchmark results (Asset Hub archive\
    \ node, 345 recorded RPC calls, 4 runtime versions)\n- Parallel replay: ~9s faster\
    \ \u2014 halving mutex acquisitions per call is a significant win under contention\n\
    - Sequential replay: neutral to slightly slower with default --runtime-cache-size=2,\
    \ due to fewer LRU promotions in the underlying `RuntimeCache`.\n\n## Changes\n\
    \n- Add `RwLock<HashMap<Vec<u8>, RuntimeVersion>>` cache to `CodeProvider`\n-\
    \ Cache hit returns cloned version via read lock; miss computes and inserts via\
    \ write lock\n- Add tests verifying cache population, reuse, and per-hash differentiation"
crates:
- name: sc-service
  bump: minor
